WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.450
Last week a file went round our

2
00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:05.070
staff WhatsApp group: “AI marking

3
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.430
app, free, no sign-up”.

4
00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.770
Three colleagues installed it.

5
00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.010
Nobody knew who made it,

6
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.390
or what else it did.

7
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.040
Today: where AI models and apps

8
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.260
come from, and how to check them

9
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.340
before you trust them.

10
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.980
Almost nobody builds AI from scratch.

11
00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.990
An app is built on a model, trained on

12
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.870
datasets, run with code libraries and

13
00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.990
plug-ins, all made by others.

14
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.720
That chain of makers is the

15
00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.460
supply chain, and any link can

16
00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:39.960
be faked or tampered with.

17
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:41.910
What can go wrong?

18
00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.940
A fake copy of a popular model,

19
00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.880
with a backdoor inside.

20
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.320
A real model, changed on the way to you.

21
00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:53.270
Or a model file in a format that runs

22
00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:55.010
code the moment you load it.

23
00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:57.640
The first check is a fingerprint.

24
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:03.220
A hash function called SHA-256 turns any

25
00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:05.260
file into sixty-four characters.

26
00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:08.690
Change a single byte, and about half

27
00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:09.910
of the fingerprint changes.

28
00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.360
In Python, it takes three lines.

29
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.140
Compute the fingerprint of the file

30
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.280
you downloaded, and compare it with

31
00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:19.420
the one the maker published.

32
00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:22.610
Same: the bytes arrived unchanged.

33
00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:25.280
Different: delete it.

34
00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:26.980
Quick check!

35
00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:30.490
The fingerprint of our download matches

36
00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:33.310
the one on the page we downloaded it from.

37
00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:34.770
Are we safe?

38
00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.820
Only if that page really

39
00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.020
belongs to the maker.

40
00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:41.790
A fingerprint proves the bytes

41
00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.230
didn't change on the way.

42
00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:46.110
It can't prove who made them: an

43
00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:47.850
impostor can publish a matching

44
00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.330
fingerprint for their own file.

45
00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:52.050
That's what a signature adds.

46
00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.020
The maker signs the file with a

47
00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:57.740
private key, and anyone can check it

48
00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.320
with the maker's public key.

49
00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.040
A valid signature says: this

50
00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:03.440
really came from them.

51
00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.460
Then build habits around it.

52
00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:09.450
Download only from the maker's official

53
00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.650
page or an official app store.

54
00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.550
Prefer model files that hold only numbers.

55
00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:18.700
And keep a list of every AI tool

56
00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.260
the school uses: name, version,

57
00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:22.880
source and fingerprint.

58
00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:26.770
In the app, check a model file three

59
00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:29.590
ways: genuine, with one byte

60
00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:32.190
changed, and from an impostor.

61
00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.140
Watch which check catches which.

62
00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:37.230
Your turn.

63
00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.950
That free marking app from the

64
00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:41.870
staff group: what do we do now?

65
00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.520
Uninstall it, and use only tools from

66
00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.660
official sources on the school's list.

67
00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:51.350
Remember: AI comes through a supply chain.

68
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.980
A fingerprint shows the bytes are

69
00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:57.440
unchanged, and a signature shows who made

70
00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:57.680
them.

71
00:02:58.300 --> 00:02:59.720
Keep a list of what you run.

72
00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.340
Try it in class tomorrow:

73
00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:03.840
make a paper fingerprint.

74
00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:07.270
Pupils write a long number, add up

75
00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:09.290
its digits and keep the total.

76
00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:12.330
A partner changes one digit in secret,

77
00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:14.470
and the new total gives it away.
